ls and cultural events also pop up from…"],["South-east Asia Center","sight",41.97529,-87.66004,"5120 N Broadway St, 1124 W Ainslie","Mon-Fri 8:30AM-5:30PM","","","","r","Not a tourist sight, necessarily, but a center for the local South-east Asian community, young and old. Ten languages (besides English) are spoken by the staff. Volunteer opportunities like English teaching and elderly care abound."],["Neo-Futurarium","activity",41.97587,-87.6692,"5153 N Ashland Ave","Fri Sat 11:30PM, Sun 7PM, closed last two weeks of December","","","","r","Andersonville — and the second floor of the Nelson Funeral Home, to be precise — was the home of the long-running late-night show Too Much Light Makes The Baby Go Blind and its ever-changing menu of the funny, the profound, and the…"],["Palace Gate","restaurant",41.96499,-87.66136,"4548 N Magnolia Ave","Mon-Wed 10AM-8PM, Thu-Sun 10AM-9PM","","","","r","In Ghana, it's considered a taboo to eat in public without inviting others to join you, so don't come to Palace Gate looking for solitude with your fufu dumplings. The decor is plastic and basic, but the atmosphere is merry."],["Svea","restaurant",41.9773,-87.66851,"5236 N Clark St","Mon-Fri 7AM-2:30PM, Sat Sun 7AM-3:30PM","","","","r","Swedish breakfast spot with renowned lingonberry pancakes."],["Kopi","bar",41.9786,-87.66814,"5317 N Clark St","Mon-Thu 8AM-11PM, Fri 8AM-midnight, Sat 9AM-midnight, Sun 10AM-11PM","","","","r","Describes itself as \"a traveler's cafe.\" In practice, it's a relaxed coffee shop of the early 1990s vintage, with earthy decor and earnest staff. Also includes a small shop of eclectic things from around the world."],["Hopleaf","bar",41.97582,-87.66853,"5148 N Clark St","Sun-Fri 3PM-2AM, Sat 3PM-3AM","","","","r","Fantastic selection of beer, with a surprisingly accessible menu for delving into the world of Belgians and local microbrews. The food is great, especially the steamed mussels, but the beer is even better. It's pricey, though. Make sure…"]]}